{
  "cup": 133,
  "source": "leaderboard screenshots shared in chat",
  "aliases": {
    "rtm_lover2007": "Kernkob"
  },
  "notes": [
    "COTD 133 predates the saved mod logs, so every round here comes from a screenshot.",
    "Serpent's Lair by [CTR]Rourie13, 2026-02-28, won by justMaki over [FPV]PandaMane in a 17 round final. All 17 rounds are screenshot confirmed and every elimination they show",
    "agrees with the elimination records, round for round.",
    "",
    "",
    "Kernkob raced this one as rtm_lover2007 and under no other name, which is why the alias",
    "above exists. The elimination records carry the same mapping.",
    "",
    "Field: 55 in the lobby, 54 racers once the mapper is out. The elimination records take that",
    "54 down to 49, 43, 37 and 31 after rounds 1 to 4.",
    "",
    "The Cup Leaderboard header does NOT identify the round. It is read off whenever Lexer opens",
    "the board during the podium sequence, which can be before or after that round's eliminations",
    "are processed, so the same number can mean two different rounds. Rounds 7 and 8 both read",
    "18 of 55 for exactly that reason. Round numbers here come from aizpun watching the cup back.",
    "",
    "Round 2 is the in round HUD, top 5 of 49. Every other round so far is a Cup Leaderboard",
    "top 16 of a larger field, so the tail of each round is unknown. That is enough for round",
    "leaders, which is what this file is for.",
    "",
    "Times here are the board's three decimals, but the game ranks on the full float behind them, so two rows can print the same number without being tied. Round 8 does that: [SWMG]JakeAdjacent and RoundNzt both show 45.499 and JakeAdjacent is genuinely ahead. Where that happens the printed order is the authority, and rows here keep board order.",
    "",
    "Round 9 is complete, all 14 racers, because it came as two shots of the same board, one before its eliminations were processed and one after. The red rows in those shots name the round each player went out in and carry more decimals than the board does, which is where round 8's times for [old]Warsnac and icRS come from, and they confirm [ZET]Stick and MALIYO as the two eliminated in round 9, matching the elimination records.",
    "",
    "Round 14's board shows Hydro last with no rank and no time, so he is recorded as null rather than DNF: the screenshot cannot tell a DNF from a run that had not finished when it was taken. Either way he is the one the records have going out in round 14.",
    "",
    "Round 15 is not a fair read of Kernkob's pace. Per aizpun, who watched the cup back, he was uncomfortable about how far he had gone on an alt account and threw the round deliberately, switching from his usual keyboard to a controller so he would not take a medal as rtm_lover2007. His 46.58483 is over a second off the 45.3s he had been running. [SWMG]JakeAdjacent then DNF'd the semi, and justMaki took the final."
  ],
